<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Sweeflow third-party licences</title>
<style>
  body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 52rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 0.8rem; border-radius: 6px; }
  .used-by { font-size: 13px; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background: #16161a; color: #ddd; } pre { background: #232329; } a { color: #9ab; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Sweeflow third-party licences</h1>
<p>Sweeflow itself is MIT licensed. It is built from the Rust crates below, each under the licence shown.
It also loads FFmpeg and other system libraries at run time; those are separate packages with their own licences.</p>

<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2>Licences</h2>
<ul class="licenses">
{{#each licenses}}
  <li class="license" id="{{id}}">
    <h3>{{name}}</h3>
    <h4>Used by</h4>
    <ul class="used-by">
    {{#each used_by}}
      <li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}{{#if crate.repository}} (<a href="{{crate.repository}}">{{crate.repository}}</a>){{/if}}</li>
    {{/each}}
    </ul>
    <pre>{{text}}</pre>
  </li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<!--SLINT-->
</body>
</html>
